  <section|Finding><label|finding>

  The parent snapshot already contains the five canonical proof chapters
  named in the task. The earlier audit was based on the stale isolated clone
  and incorrectly treated those chapters as missing. They were read in full
  from the parent snapshot and are recorded below. They prove substantial
  shared quantifier, history, scale, and OPE-service arguments; they do
  <strong|not> need to be recreated as packages.

  There are still two source routes, and their existential runs must not be
  identified. The chain

  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.preFoundK>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Roll/Novena.lean>) \<rightarrow\>
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.freakK>
  (<verbatim|.../Roll/Ebb.lean>) \<rightarrow\>
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.factorGK>
  (<verbatim|.../Roll/Ariva.lean>) \<rightarrow\>
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.meridian>
  (<verbatim|.../Roll/Meridian.lean>)

  is an alternate construction. <verbatim|factorGK> chooses an order profile
  with support exponent <verbatim|100+i>; <verbatim|meridian> constructs a
  run/campaign with <verbatim|Locrian>, <verbatim|Jams.Wild>, and the
  requested kernel penalty. It does not return <verbatim|R2I.Funded>, the
  native attachment, or an equality to the run from the public selector. No
  source declaration inspected transports those properties between the two
  existential witnesses. The Roll chain is therefore not an input to the
  common-history proofs unless a concrete consumer requiring it is
  identified.

  The public source route is

  <verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>) \<rightarrow\>
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodRun.lean>)
  \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.allFactorWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock.lean>)
  \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.plentifulWithPrediction>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Bardo.lean>). This is
  the witness to bind to the canonical chapters.

  <section|What the public source actually
  retains><label|what-the-public-source-actually-retains>

  <verbatim|constructionRun> calls the selector with the default dynamics,
  minted custody, <verbatim|garment10>, the input penalty
  <verbatim|b\<gtr\>0>, the trivial eventually-paid predicate,
  <verbatim|NativeComponentRecipe.available>, and the native
  floor/numeric/postnumeric requests. The selector's profile has
  <verbatim|supportExp := fun _ =\<gtr\> 100>; its output proves the exact
  parameter identity <verbatim|(A.B.a.params i).supportExponent = 100> for
  every <verbatim|i>. It separately proves the budget inequality
  <verbatim|(A.B.a.budget i).supportExponent \<geq\> 100>. Do not identify
  the exact profile equality with the budget lower bound. The Roll profile
  <verbatim|100+i> is not the source of either public fact.

  The selector's preselection keeps the sheet and quote identities
  <verbatim|R.metals.p = ThroughLaunch.raise s n> and <verbatim|R.metals.K =
  ThroughLaunch.raging s T>, the pre-length floor and native extra-floor,
  diagonal and post-length numerical paid requests, and the stage-zero
  post-length payment. It also returns order/power bounds, the treasury and
  common-period funding predicates, campaign pillars, the funded record, and
  campaign receipts.

  <verbatim|ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.of_preselection> applies
  <verbatim|.on_run> to that same run. <verbatim|on_run> derives the kernel,
  stage, and factor equalities from <verbatim|R.alloy.B.valid>, transfers the
  pre-length floor with <verbatim|R.rolls.large>, then calls
  <verbatim|NativeComponentRecipe.realize> on the actual
  <verbatim|R.family.path.levels> and <verbatim|R.alloy.B.M>, using
  <verbatim|R.alloy.B.plan>. Thus the <verbatim|Attached R> returned by
  <verbatim|constructionRun> is genuinely same-clock/same-horizon data,
  including the native flat, dual, sworn, and Redo/Yamen receipts.

  There is one actual wrapper-erasure issue.
  <verbatim|selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>
  returns, in order, the exact penalty, preselection, order/power bounds, the
  selected eventually-paid predicate, <verbatim|CalendarTreasuryPurchase.TreasuryFunded>,
  <verbatim|CommonPeriodPurchase.Funded>, campaign pillars,
  <verbatim|R2I.Funded>, and additional receipts. <verbatim|constructionRun>
  destructures this result with anonymous placeholders for the order/power,
  selected predicate, treasury, and common-period fields. Its stated
  conclusion retains the same <verbatim|R,T,W>, penalty, <verbatim|R2I.Funded
  (garment10 G) R T>, and <verbatim|Attached R>, but not those four
  standalone witnesses.

  The missing treasury and common-period proofs are available at the
  underlying selector call in the proof body; they are not mathematical
  consequences one may simply recover from the <verbatim|Funded> record. The
  correct bridge is to preserve/name the required selector witnesses at the
  composition step (or add a strengthened wrapper theorem). Do not assert
  that <verbatim|constructionRun>'s current theorem statement alone provides
  them. The same caution applies to any downstream use of the discarded
  order/power or eventually-paid outputs.

  <section|Canonical chapter comparison><label|canonical-chapter-comparison>

  These chapters exist at the parent checkpoint and were read directly. They
  settle the mathematical scheduling/assembly joins; the remaining task is to
  bind their inputs to the native selector without duplicating their proofs.

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Canonical
  chapter>>|<cell|<strong|What it already proves>>|<cell|<strong|Remaining
  source binding>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|common-funded-history.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:common-funded-history>>|<cell|Simultaneous quantifier order
  for profiles, block lengths, prices/protection, delays, menus, and scale
  realization; retention of stationary and free data on one realization;
  exact tail identities after terminal normalization; same local return for
  every interval; explicit price comparison and continuation of retained
  histories. It states its analytic suppliers as prerequisites and does not
  claim numerical scale selection substitutes for them.>|<cell|Bind its
  realized profiles, path/history, and purchases to the single public
  <verbatim|R,T,W>. Preserve treasury/common-period outputs if the common
  floor list consumes them; do not attempt to derive them from
  <verbatim|R2I.Funded> alone.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|common-observable-purchases.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:common-observable-purchases>>|<cell|Makes observable,
  differentiated, multi-insertion, and localization purchases on the same
  selected history, with common dictionaries and finite-volume uniformity;
  explicitly says it does not choose a second solution of the shooting
  problem. It honestly leaves simultaneous global assembly to the
  centered-service/UV section.>|<cell|Identify its common history with
  <verbatim|R.family> and its campaign/paths with <verbatim|T,W> from the
  public selector. <verbatim|constructionRun> returns these together with
  <verbatim|Funded> and <verbatim|Attached>; no Roll witness is
  needed.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|common-scale-selection.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:common-scale-selection>>|<cell|Gives the explicit slowly
  advancing scale sequence, long plateaux, period choices, countable and
  all-stage payments, and ordering of length floors before post-length costs.
  It explicitly leaves analytic hypotheses to their suppliers.>|<cell|Match
  the fixed profile and required floors/costs to the native selected
  order/profile and actual clock factors. The selector does return these
  receipts, but the current public wrapper discards some of them as
  above.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|ope-scale-purchases.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:ope-scale-purchases>>|<cell|Chooses support exponent exactly
  <verbatim|100>, proves the fixed-stage halo/block-length inequalities and
  the stated intermediate-scale consequences; links these choices to the
  common funding/observable purchases.>|<cell|Exact support profile is
  supplied by the native selector's <verbatim|(A.B.a.params
  i).supportExponent = 100>, retained in <verbatim|R2I.Funded.fixed>. Keep
  separate from the budget exponent lower bound. No Roll profile conversion
  is needed.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|ope-history-service.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:ope-history-service>>|<cell|Proves finite elementary
  representation transport, several-insertion allowances, and uniformity
  above each reference level on one adjacent transition; it explicitly keeps
  the same background transition and history.>|<cell|Apply it to the same
  <verbatim|R,T,W> and fixed-exponent <verbatim|Funded> record. The source
  has <verbatim|R2I.Funded.gallery>, <verbatim|.logPackage>, and
  <verbatim|YM.R2IGoals.fromFunded>; these are the exact output-side
  projections. Do not silently drop <verbatim|W>, which <verbatim|logPackage>
  and <verbatim|fromFunded> use.>>>>>

  The four common/OPE joins therefore are not five missing mathematical
  arguments: the canonical chapters prove the shared construction and
  same-history claims. The remaining prose/source boundary is a short
  witness-preservation and assumption-map task, with the explicit
  wrapper-erasure caveat above. Overall construction estimates and analytic
  suppliers remain separately tracked by their own chapters; this audit does
  not upgrade their status.

  <section|Recommended disjoint packages><label|recommended-disjoint-packages>

  These are source-binding prose/evidence tasks only. No upstream Lean change
  is proposed in this #26 writing task.

  <subsection|Package A \V Preserve the native selector
  witnesses><label|package-a--preserve-the-native-selector-witnesses>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><strong|Output:> <verbatim|manuscript/existence/public-run-binding.tex>
    and <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/public-run-binding-evidence.md>.

    <item><strong|Source interface:> <verbatim|constructionRun>;
    <verbatim|selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>;
    <verbatim|allFactorWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>;
    <verbatim|NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock>;
    <verbatim|ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.{PostnumericPreselection,Attached,on_run,of_preselection}>;
    <verbatim|NativeComponentRecipe.{Choice,Realized,realize}>.

    <item><strong|Task:> record the exact same <verbatim|R,T,W>, fixed
    profile exponent, distinct budget exponent bound, sheet/quote/length
    identities, numerical requests, actual clock/horizon realization, and
    native attachment. Name and retain the selector's treasury,
    common-period, order/power, and predicate outputs if consumed by the
    parent theorem; otherwise say that the current wrapper drops them. The
    proof is composition of already-existing records, not a new construction
    estimate.

    <item><strong|Dependencies:> the five canonical chapters listed above and
    the current <verbatim|rg-construction.tex>,
    <verbatim|rg-horizon-geometry.tex>, and their evidence.

    <item><strong|Consumer:> Packages already present; it supplies an exact
    source-to-hypothesis map rather than new math for their conclusions.
  </itemize-minus>

  <subsection|Package B \V Source crosswalk for common-history and OPE
  applications><label|package-b--source-crosswalk-for-common-history-and-ope-applications>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><strong|Output:> a short subsection in
    <verbatim|public-run-binding.tex> (or a crosswalk table in its evidence
    file), not a duplicate proof chapter.

    <item><strong|Source interface:> <verbatim|R2I.Funded.{gallery,coverage,logPackage}>,
    <verbatim|YM.R2IGoals.fromFunded>, plus <verbatim|constructionRun>'s
    <verbatim|R,T,W,Funded,Attached> result.

    <item><strong|Task:> map each actual field to the hypothesis consumed in
    <verbatim|common-funded-history>, <verbatim|common-observable-purchases>,
    <verbatim|common-scale-selection>, <verbatim|ope-scale-purchases>, and
    <verbatim|ope-history-service>; point at the already-proved labels above.
    Explicitly state that the retained <verbatim|W> is required for OPE
    service and that trace/observable predicates are on <verbatim|R.family>.

    <item><strong|Dependencies:> Package A and the existing canonical
    chapters; no rederivation of scale recursion, local observables, or OPE
    transport.
  </itemize-minus>

  <subsection|No package for Roll/Meridian unless a consumer is
  found><label|no-package-for-rollmeridian-unless-a-consumer-is-found>

  Mark the <verbatim|preFoundK> \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|freakK>
  \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|factorGK> \<rightarrow\> <verbatim|meridian> chain
  as an alternate existence route in the source crosswalk. Replace any
  citation that uses it as a public-run supplier. Do not attempt to prove
  equality or transfer between the two existential <verbatim|Run>s absent a
  concrete consumer.

